      "writtenOn": "2020-09-08T17:27:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "err.serviceSpecificErrorCode() \u003d\u003d 0 does not imply success. You have to check err.exceptionCode() first.\n\nSee comment on serviceSpecificErrorCode in KeyMintAidlTestBase.cpp\n\nUsing std::variant this could look like this:\n\n VerificationToken verifyToken;\n\n Status err \u003d keyMint().verifyAuthorization(operationHandle,               //\n                                            paramsToVerify.vector_data(),  //\n                                            authToken,                     //\n                                            \u0026verifyToken);\n\n if (err.isOk()) return {verifyToken};\n if (err.exceptionCode() \u003d\u003d EX_SERVICE_SPECIFIC) {\n     return {static_cast\u003cErrorCode\u003e(err.serviceSpecificErrorCode())};\n }\n return {ErrorCode::UNKNOWN_ERROR};",
      "range": {
